<div class="proto-notes" id="proto-notes" role="dialog" aria-label="Design notes">
<h3>One link, one place</h3>
<p>An organisation receives a program only through program assignment: step 2 of Add organisation, or Assign program on a Draft organisation. Programs never hold organisation, region, funder or date details. Those belong to the assignment.</p>
<h3>Programs are reusable and versioned</h3>
<p>Sawit360 ships with predefined programs, and the Super Admin can create new ones or change existing ones. Every change creates a new version. Organisations stay on their version until the Super Admin moves them. To change one organisation only, duplicate the program and assign the copy.</p>
<h3>More than one entry point</h3>
<p>Farmers can join a program at more than one pillar. For example, RISS Certification Journey lets farmers join at Diffusion or at Traceability &amp; Verification. The Super Admin marks the entry points in Create program, and farmers who join at a later pillar still get their master farmer ID from Traceability &amp; Verification.</p>
<h3>Group Managers are set per program</h3>
<p>When building a program, the Super Admin decides whether it uses Group Managers, which pillars each Group Manager role covers, and whether Ketua Bahagian work under it. A role can cover one pillar or several. On the field, Certification &amp; Compliance usually has a Group Manager, and the same Group Manager usually covers Livelihood Improvement too, because LI collects data that CC needs for certification. Group Managers are community members, and each Ketua Bahagian looks after 20 to 35 farms. Pillars without a Group Manager are run by CSS Field Officers.</p>
<h3>Two kinds of documents</h3>
<p>First login documents belong to the organisation: Terms of Use and Privacy Notice for everyone, a confidentiality undertaking for all users except farmers, and appointment letters for Group Managers and Ketua Bahagian. Journey documents come from the program and are signed when a farmer moves into a pillar: Consent Form (DF), Participatory Agreement (TV), Membership Form and Smallholder Declaration (CC), and LoU Fertilizer Program (LI). A journey document can be carried forward, so a farmer who joins at a later pillar still signs it. Documents can be added or removed for a program (Create program, Documents step, including brand new documents) or for one organisation only (Add organisation step 5 and the Documents tab). A new document starts as a draft and needs approval. Removing a document keeps every signed copy.</p>
<h3>About this prototype</h3>
<p style="margin:0">All data is sample data. Buttons, tabs, filters, links and the sidebar work, so each flow can be clicked through.</p>
